#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096479 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096680 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7ffce8b3-cc12-5a4d-88fd-77889b6bdd3f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating a Trigonometric Expression Using the Tabular Method of Integration by Parts"}] :question/id #uuid "f4bca758-9903-505c-9828-0e1788b25d9f" :question/math-academy-id "e-499" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int (x^4-3x) \\cos(x) \\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "For this integral we choose $u = x^4-3x$ and\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}v}{\\textrm{d}x} = \\cos(x)\n$$\n\nFilling in the table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} x^4-3x$ | $\\cos(x)$ |  |  |\n| $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06} 4x^3-3$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} \\sin(x)$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} +$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} (x^4-3x)\\sin(x)$ |\n| $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1} 12x^2$ | $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06} -\\cos(x)$ | $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06} -$ | $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06} -(4x^3-3)(-\\cos(x))$ |\n| $\\color[rgb]{1,0,1} 24x$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1} -\\sin(x)$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1} +$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1} 12x^2(-\\sin(x))$ |\n| $\\color[rgb]{0,0.5,1} 24$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,1} \\cos(x)$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,1} -$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,1}- 24x\\cos(x)$ |\n| $0$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0.5,1} \\sin(x)$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0.5,1}+$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0.5,1} 24\\sin(x)$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int(x^{4} - 3x)\\cos (x)dx &= (x^{4} - 3x)\\sin (x) + (4x^{3} - 3)\\cos (x) \\\\\n&=-12x^{2}\\sin (x) - 24x\\cos (x) + 24\\sin (x) + C \\\\\n&= (x^{4} - 12x^{2} - 3x + 24)\\sin (x) \\\\\n&= + (4x^{3} - 24x - 3)\\cos (x) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096482 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096681 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "708faaf1-be43-502c-88dc-94270e8783b6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Algebraic and Exponential Expressions Using the Tabular Method of Integration by Parts"}] :question/id #uuid "96f1c791-f1cd-5a20-a6ee-004475bbd482" :question/math-academy-id "e-500" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int (x^2-1)(x+2)^5 \\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "For this integral, we choose $u = x^2-1$ and\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}v}{\\textrm{d}x} =(x+2)^5\n$$\n\nFilling in our table gives the following:\n\n| **Derivatives** | **Integrals** | **Sign** | **Same-color Products** |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} x^2-1$ | $(x+2)^5$ |  |  |\n| $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06} 2x$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\\dfrac{(x+2)^6}{6}$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0} +$ | $\\color[rgb]{1,0,0}\\dfrac{(x^2-1)(x+2)^6}{6}$ |\n| $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1} 2$ | $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06} \\dfrac{(x+2)^7}{42}$ | $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06} -$ | $\\color[rgb]{0.77,0.45,0.06} -\\,\\dfrac{x(x+2)^7}{21}$ |\n| $0$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1}\\dfrac{(x+2)^8}{336}$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1} +$ | $\\color[rgb]{0,0,1} \\dfrac{(x+2)^8}{168}$ |\n\nWe add up all the terms of the last column to get the answer for our integral.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int(x^{2} - 1)(x + 2)^{5}dx &= ((x^{2} - 1)(x + 2)^{6})/(6) - (x(x + 2)^{7})/(21) + ((x + 2)^{8})/(168) + C \\\\\n&= ((x + 2)^{6})/(168)(28(x^{2} - 1) - 8x(x + 2) + (x + 2)^{2}) + C \\\\\n&= ((x + 2)^{6})/(168)(21x^{2} - 12x - 24) + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097127 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096681 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "708faaf1-be43-502c-88dc-94270e8783b6" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Algebraic and Exponential Expressions Using the Tabular Method of Integration by Parts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94be014b-aea3-515f-8461-3c53a2d443d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{x}(3x^{4} - 12x^{3} - 48x^{2} - 96x + 98) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 1759